`(offset, instruction, length)` each, in the `SegVC.Listing Open9.isa` shape. Generated by
running `Open9.decode` along the code (a throwaway generator script, a linear sweep: the code
has no embedded data) and checked against the bytes by `adlerListing_valid`
(`decide +kernel`). The five `imul $0xfff1, r/m64, r64` (offsets `0x183`, `0x1aa`, `0x25e`,
`0x418`, `0x43f`) are `Ext9` forms; everything else is an `X86.Ext` form.
-/

